    {
        "id": "sitl02-tab",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "SITL 02 Completion timeout",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Deliberately provoke completion-tier timeout: arm, confirm GUIDED, then command an 80 m takeoff with a 3 s completion timeout. The takeoff should be ACCEPTED, but the vehicle should not reach altitude before the completion timer expires.",
        "env": []
    },
    {
        "id": "sitl02-comment",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "sitl02-tab",
        "name": "Accepted takeoff that cannot complete before timeout",
        "info": "The chain prepares the vehicle with completion-checked arm and GUIDED commands, then asks for an 80 m takeoff using delivery=complete and completionTimeout=3000. ArduPilot should ACK the takeoff, but 80 m is intentionally unreachable in 3 seconds, so output 1 reports the completion timeout and output 0 stays silent.\n\nLaunch (single ArduCopter sysid 1):\n  sim_vehicle.py -v ArduCopter --out=udp:127.0.0.1:14550\n\nConnection: bind 0.0.0.0:14550, remote 127.0.0.1:14551. The harness also preps sysid 1 into GUIDED so this story tests completion timeout, not immediate DENIED.",
        "x": 250,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
